      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Begin by thoroughly documenting all the current encroachments, the proposed design, and how it conflicts with the municipal code. You may want to consult with a professional who can help interpret the zoning laws and propose a solution. With this information, schedule a meeting with the city planning commission to present your case, offering alternatives if possible and highlighting how your proposal aligns with the city's values and development goals. Be prepared to negotiate and show flexibility while also making a persuasive argument for keeping your reclassification request on track.",
